@startuml review_report_00_baseline
' Review unit 00 of 02 -- see docs/review_report.md for the series.
' State AT commit f87a0e9, main after PR #22, where the rebased branch starts.
' Every number below is from a run of the cases at commit f87a0e9.
' Render: plantuml docs/review_report_00_baseline.puml

title Unit 00 -- baseline: the data flow when the branch starts (f87a0e9)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #777777
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  DiamondBorderColor #777777
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #8899AA
  FontColor #33495E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #C8C08A
}

start

partition "the call" {
  :GenerateData(
     num_obs=100, num_dims=3, ratio_dims=[1, 2, 2],
     density=[0.4, 0.1], seed=77,
     num_vars=2, var_dims=[3, 2],
     overlap=0.5, fixed_overlap=False,
     <b>case A</b>: max_obs=None      <b>case B</b>: max_obs=40)
  .generate(netcdf_filepath, parquet_filepath,
     parquet_tmp, merge_nc=True);
}

partition "validate and configure" {
  :validators rewrite the request, and print both versions
  num_obs 100 -> 102, shape [4, 8, 8] (256 sites)
  var_num_obs 102 and 26, var1 on (x1, x2), pinned on x0
  dim_split 1, NTASKS 1 (A) or 3 (B);
  note right
    The constructor arguments are not kept.
    After validation only the corrected
    values exist on the instance, so nothing
    can later compare them with the request.
  end note
}

partition "place and store" {
  :stratified placement, var0 then var1
  OverlapCalculator: F1 0.4561 for a target of 0.5
  WARNING var1: overlap target not reachable in 5 of 8 strata
  VariableEncoding.to_stored (float64 by default: unchanged);
}

if (NTASKS) then (== 1  -- CASE A, serial)
  :build DataArray / Dataset and DataFrame in memory
  write ds.nc 15729 B and the parquet
  return (Dataset, DataFrame);
else (== 3  -- CASE B, parallel)
  :ProcessPoolExecutor, generate_chunk(**args) per chunk
  each worker places its strata, writes its files, and returns
  <b>(chunk_id, total_obs, parquet_chunk_path)</b>;
  :parent sums total_obs, consolidates the parquet,
  merges the netCDF (ds.nc 13558 B)
  return (None, None): the data exist only on disk;
endif

#FFF9C4:what the user learns at the end of the run:
the corrected configuration and the overlap warning.
No statement of how the OUTPUT compares with the REQUEST:
occupied cells, density reached, coverage, whether the
two formats hold the same number of values;

partition "two more cases the later units use" {
  :<b>single variable</b>: num_vars=1, density=0.4
  102 values, ds.nc 14061 B;
  :<b>case S</b> (saturation): density=[0.4, 0.4], var_dims=[[0, 1, 2], [1, 2]] --
  var1 asks for 0.4 * 256 = 102 sites but lives on a 64-cell (x1, x2)
  grid: it is capped at 64, every cell filled, F1 1.0. Nothing says so;
}

stop

legend right
  |<#C8E6C9> green |= added or changed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFCDD2> red |= removed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFE0B2> orange |= single-variable flow touched by THIS unit |
  |<#FFF9C4> yellow |= generated data or file that changed as a result |
  | plain | unchanged since the previous unit |

  <b>Unit 00 is the reference</b>, not a change.
  Serial equals parallel in every case: same decoded
  netCDF, same parquet rows.
end legend

@enduml
